  { q: "If I turn off auto-renew, does Premium stop right away?", a: "No. Turning off auto-renew only stops the next charge — the period you already paid for runs all the way to its end date. If you have 15 days left, every Premium feature keeps working for those 15 days." },
  { q: "Do I get a partial refund for the days I don't use?", a: "No. Under standard App Store and Google Play terms, cancelling mid-period does not trigger a partial refund — the amount you paid covers the full period regardless of when you cancel." },
  { q: "What if the cancel option is greyed out or missing?", a: "This is usually a device or account mismatch: if you subscribed on Android and later switched to an iPhone, the subscription is still managed by Google Play, so you need to sign into that same Google account (on any device or browser) to cancel it. Telegram Desktop and Web also generally do not show a cancel button for a subscription bought on mobile." },
  { q: "Do I need to cancel Premium bought through StarsJoy?", a: "No. A StarsJoy purchase is a one-off Stars or card payment, not a recurring subscription that charges your card automatically. There is nothing to cancel — when the term ends, you simply buy again only if you want to." },
