  <section>
    <p class="post-lead"><strong>Short answer:</strong> to turn off Telegram Premium auto-renewal, you need to know how it was paid for. On iOS: <strong>Settings &gt; your name &gt; Subscriptions</strong>. On Android: <strong>Google Play &gt; Payments &amp; subscriptions</strong>. Paid with Stars through Telegram's own @PremiumBot: send <strong>/stop</strong> in that chat. Premium bought through a reseller bot like StarsJoy never auto-renews in the first place, so there's nothing to cancel.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p>This guide is not about what happens when Premium <strong>runs out on its own</strong> — that's covered in <a href="/en/blog/telegram-premium-expired">what happens when Telegram Premium expires</a>. This is about <strong>actively turning off</strong> the recurring charge, so your card isn't billed again next month.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why turn off auto-renewal in the first place?</h2>
    <p>The most common reasons: deciding to stop using Premium, switching to a different payment method, or simply wanting control over what gets charged to a card every month. Whatever the reason, the process depends on exactly where the subscription was purchased — Telegram itself cannot manage these charges directly, because they run through the App Store or Google Play.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to cancel on iOS (App Store)</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open <strong>Settings</strong> on your iPhone.</li>
      <li>Tap your name (<strong>Apple ID</strong>) at the top.</li>
      <li>Go to <strong>Subscriptions</strong>.</li>
      <li>Find <strong>Telegram Premium</strong> in the list and tap it.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Cancel Subscription</strong> and confirm.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Alternative route: open the App Store app, tap your profile icon in the top-right corner, choose <strong>Subscriptions</strong>, find Telegram in the list, and cancel there.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to cancel on Android (Google Play)</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the <strong>Google Play</strong> app.</li>
      <li>Tap your profile icon in the top-right corner.</li>
      <li>Choose <strong>Payments &amp; subscriptions &gt; Subscriptions</strong>.</li>
      <li>Find <strong>Telegram</strong> in the list.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Cancel subscription</strong> and confirm.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>After cancelling, Google Play still shows the end date — that just means Premium keeps working until the current paid period is over.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What if I subscribed with Stars through @PremiumBot?</h2>
    <p>A Premium subscription set up as a monthly plan through Telegram's own official <strong>@PremiumBot</strong>, paid with Stars, also auto-renews — it deducts the right amount of Stars from your balance every month. To turn this off, open the chat with <strong>@PremiumBot</strong> and send the <strong>/stop</strong> command.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Can I cancel from Desktop or Web?</h2>
    <p>Telegram Desktop and Telegram Web show your Premium status, but they generally do not show a cancel button for a subscription bought on mobile (App Store/Google Play) — only the system that actually took the payment can manage it. So cancelling always happens on whichever platform you originally paid through: your phone's settings, or the bot chat.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="post-cta-box">
